(vector (map (:registry/operating-states (vector :intake :propose :approve :execute :audit)), (:actor/wave 3), (:registry/required-technologies (vector :robotics :identity :audit-ledger)), (:actor/scope-excluded-ops (vector :finalize-assembly-decision :finalize-assembly-operation :authorize-assembly-run :proceed-with-assembly-run :finalize-line-safety-clearance :declare-line-safety-cleared :declare-board-safe-for-handling :declare-assembled-batch-safe-for-handling :declare-batch-safe-for-shipment :clear-batch-for-shipment :override-plant-safety-officer-judgment :override-safety-officer-judgment)), (:actor/robotics? true), (:adr/related (vector "adr-2607121000-cloud-itonami-global-isic-isco-reverse-toposort-plan" "adr-2799008122-cloud-itonami-isco-8122-metal-finishing-plating-coating-machine-operators-coverage")), (:adr/status :accepted), (:actor/scope-excluded-terms (vector "proceed with the assembly run" "proceed with the assembly operation" "authorize the assembly run" "authorize the assembly operation" "finalize the assembly decision" "finalize the assembly operation" "declare the line safety cleared" "declare the assembly line safety cleared" "declare the board safe for handling" "declare the assembled batch safe for handling" "declare the batch safe for shipment" "declare the assembled batch safe for shipment" "clear the batch for shipment" "clear the assembled batch for handling" "finalize the line safety clearance" "finalize the line-safety clearance" "override the plant safety officer's judgment" "override the safety officer's judgment" "override plant safety officer judgment")), (:adr/id 2799008212), (:phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:log-work-record :flag-safety-concern :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order}, :auto #{:log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation}}}"), (:actor/domain :manufacturing/electrical-electronic-equipment-assembly-scheduling-logistics-coordination), (:actor/proposal-ops (vector :log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order)), (:actor/hard-checks (vector :no-worker :no-line :no-actuation :unknown-op :scope-excluded-action)), (:registry/maturity :implemented), (:actor/isco-08 "8212"), (:actor/always-escalate-ops (vector :flag-safety-concern)), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:operation/nodes (vector :intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold)), (:operation/entry-point :intake), (:adr/body "# ADR 2799008212: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 8212 Electrical and Electronic Equipment Assemblers assembly-line scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 8212\n-- Electrical and Electronic Equipment Assemblers** only. This is\nWave3 (production/trades); Wave0/1/2 are 100% complete and the 75xx\ncraft-trades range and much of the 81xx/82xx plant-and-machine-operator\nrange are already complete; this batch is part of the 82xx assemblers\nsubgroup (`kotoba.occupation.wave/wave-of \"8212\"` resolves to wave 3).\n\n`gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8212` returned a clean\n404 before any work began -- this was a genuinely fresh scaffold, not a\nresume of prior partial work.\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"8212\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"8212\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Electrical and Electronic\nEquipment Assemblers\" -- confirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior to\nthis ADR the entry's `:maturity` was `:spec` with\n`:required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger]` and no\n`:repo`/`:business-id`. This ADR and its companion registry edit\npromote the `8212` entry to `:implemented`.\n\n**Electrical/ESD assembly-line hazard dimension.** Electrical and\nElectronic Equipment Assemblers assemble circuit boards and electrical\nequipment on production lines -- a real electrical-shock hazard,\nalongside an ESD (electrostatic discharge)-sensitive component-\nhandling hazard (mishandling can silently damage components or, in\nrarer cases, ignite sensitive materials). This actor does NOT model\ndirect assembly-execution authority or line-safety-clearance\nauthority. It is deliberately restricted to LINE SCHEDULING and\nLOGISTICS COORDINATION around the occupation (production-run/\ninventory/progress-record logging, crew/shift scheduling, safety-\nconcern escalation, and electronic-components-stock procurement\ncoordination) -- never the assembly-execution decision or the\nline-safety-clearance decision itself, and never an override of a\nplant safety officer's judgment. The closed proposal-op allowlist\nstructurally excludes any op that could directly finalize such a\ndecision, and the governor independently, permanently hard-blocks any\nproposal whose rationale text names such a finalization action,\nregardless of the declared `:op` or confidence -- this is not an\nescalation path a human can approve through, it is an outright,\nstructural refusal at every maturity level.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8122`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8122)\n(Metal Finishing, Plating and Coating Machine Operators -- a closely\nrelated assembly-line safety-coordination pattern; the originally\nsuggested reference `cloud-itonami-isco-8211`, Mechanical Machinery\nAssemblers, did not yet exist at the time this repo was scaffolded, so\n8122 was used per the task's documented fallback), independently\nre-cloned and read in full this session. Its\n`platingcoord.{store,advisor,governor,actor}` module split,\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph shape, closed op-allowlist and\nscope-exclusion self-trip-guard design translate almost 1:1 onto this\noccupation's own assembly-line-coordination scope, so this ADR's\n`elecassemblycoord.*` modules follow the same shape with domain terms\nsubstituted (plater -> worker, plating facility/plant -> assembly\nline, plating-operation-execution -> assembly-execution, chemical-\nsafety-clearance -> line-safety-clearance).\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8212` as an OSS\ndocumentation/logistics-coordination actor for electrical and\nelectronic equipment assemblers, following the SAME governed-actor\narchitecture as every prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this\nfleet: **Electrical/Electronic Assembly Line Scheduling Coordination\nAdvisor ⊣ ElecAssemblyCoordGovernor** on a `langgraph.graph`\nStateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`, git-sha-pinned\nidentically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- a different library\ncoordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated\n`20-actors/*` actor family), with an independent Governor,\nhuman-in-the-loop approval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only\naudit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **line scheduling/logistics coordination\nONLY, never assembly-execution authority** -- it must NEVER be\ndesigned to exercise, simulate exercising, or propose exercising an\nassembly-execution decision or a line-safety-clearance decision.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- production-run/inventory/progress data\n  logging only\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/shift/task scheduling proposal\n  only\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface an electrical-hazard/ESD-\n  condition/equipment-condition concern, ALWAYS escalates\n  immediately, NEVER auto-commit-eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- electronic-components-stock\n  procurement proposal only\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase,\nresembles an assembly-execution finalization decision or a\nline-safety-clearance finalization decision -- these are structurally\nabsent from the op-allowlist entirely, not merely gated behind\nescalation.\n\n### Five HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Worker unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered worker (crew member) record\n   (`:no-worker`). Never trusts the proposal's own claim of who the\n   worker is.\n2. **Line unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered assembly-line record (`:no-line`).\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (`:no-actuation`; the governor never dispatches hardware\n   itself and never performs assembly work itself).\n4. **Op not allowed** -- any `:op` outside the closed four-op\n   allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`).\n5. **Scope-excluded action** -- the proposal's `:op` or `:rationale`\n   must never name an assembly-execution finalization, a\n   line-safety-clearance finalization, or a plant-safety-officer-\n   judgment override (`:scope-excluded-action`), REGARDLESS of the\n   declared `:op` or confidence. This is a hard, PERMANENT block --\n   there is no maturity level or confidence at which this actor may\n   auto-commit or human-approve its way past this rule; it is an\n   outright refusal, not an escalation.\n\n### Escalation gates (always human sign-off)\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's always-escalate path). The only channel by\n  which the robot may surface an electrical-shock/ESD-condition/\n  equipment-condition observation -- it never resolves the concern\n  itself.\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000) -- always needs human sign-off,\n  independent of confidence (boundary verified as exclusive by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`: exactly-at-threshold\n  commits, over-threshold escalates).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, CLAUDE.md)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as bare NOUNS (e.g.\n\"circuit board\", \"ESD\", \"voltage\") can accidentally match inside the\nmock advisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate proposal,\nself-blocking the actor's own happy path -- and this vertical's domain\nvocabulary is an especially sharp case of that risk, because routine\nwork-log/task text legitimately names circuit-board assembly and ESD-\nsensitive components by name (e.g. a task literally described as\n\"routine circuit board assembly task with ESD-sensitive components\nunder line voltage\" -- component identification, not a proposal to\nfinalize an assembly operation or clear a line as safe).\n`elecassemblycoord.governor/scope-excluded-phrases` is phrased\nexclusively as finalization ACTION PHRASES (\"proceed with the assembly\nrun\", \"finalize the assembly operation\", \"declare the line safety\ncleared\", \"override the plant safety officer's judgment\"), never bare\nnouns, and is checked only against the proposal's `:rationale` field\n(the advisor's own generated text), never against raw `:task` input\ntext. `elecassemblycoord.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-\nnever-self-trip-on-scope-exclusion` is a dedicated regression test\ndriving the default mock-advisor across all four allowed ops with a\ntask field containing exactly those bare component/hazard nouns,\nasserting none of them ever hard-trip the finalization-scope rule.\nGreen on first run.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"8212\" ...}` entry\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8212` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-8212`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary` immediately before the edit,\n  not assumed, to account for concurrent sibling landings in this same\n  batch).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 33 tests, 71 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's `:test/\n  counts` and independently re-verified against a brand-new fresh\n  clone of the pushed repository (not just the local working copy). No\n  mojibake in the Japanese violation-detail strings (0\n  replacement-byte instances grepped in the fresh clone).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely\n  via the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent\n  with sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`) -- a single-entity EDN vector with an\n  `:adr/body` string blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-assembly-run`/`:approve-line-\n  safety-clearance` that is merely gated behind an always-escalate\n  path: rejected outright per the task's explicit guidance -- an\n  always-escalate op still means the *capability* to finalize an\n  assembly operation or a line-safety clearance exists in the code\n  path and is merely deferred to a human gate. For a decision whose\n  failure mode is electrical shock or ESD-driven component/equipment\n  damage, the capability itself must not exist in this actor at all.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"circuit board\" \"ESD\"\n  \"voltage\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known self-trip bug\n  class described above, and per this task's explicit CRITICAL\n  warning -- this domain's own vocabulary necessarily discusses\n  circuit boards, ESD sensitivity and line voltage by name to do its\n  logging/scheduling job, so a bare-noun list would self-block the\n  actor's own legitimate proposals whenever a task description\n  mentions them.\n- Naming the crew-member field `:assembler-id` (matching the ISCO\n  title \"...Equipment Assemblers\" literally): rejected -- `:worker-id`\n  (mirroring the reference's `:plater-id` pattern, generalized) keeps\n  the field name stable across sibling assembler/operator/coordinator\n  ISCO actors and avoids overloading \"assembler\" (already used\n  informally for the human occupation) with a second, narrower schema\n  meaning.\n\n## Test verification\n\nFresh clone re-run immediately before writing this ADR:\n\n```text\nRunning tests in #{\"test\"}\n\nTesting elecassemblycoord.actor-test\n\nTesting elecassemblycoord.governor-test\n\nRan 33 tests containing 71 assertions.\n0 failures, 0 errors.\n```\n"), (:adr/date "2026-07-18"), (:test/counts "{:total 33, :assertions 71, :failures 0, :errors 0}"), (:actor/coordination? true), (:actor/name "Electrical and Electronic Equipment Assembly Line Scheduling and Logistics Coordination Practice"), (:db/id -1), (:test/coverage (vector :governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :worker-verification :line-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation :assembly-execution-line-safety-clearance-finalization-forbidden :plant-safety-officer-override-forbidden)), (:registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-8212"), (:registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8212"), (:adr/scope (vector :kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8212)), (:test/simulator :elecassemblycoord.actor-test), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-8212 — Electrical and Electronic Equipment Assemblers Assembly Line Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage"), (:adr/source-format "edn"), (:adr/references (vector 2607121000)), (:actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-8212)))
